If writing the fetched chapters to the archive path fails (e.g., due to a read-only filesystem, permission issues, or disk full), `write_text` will raise an `OSError`. Since this is not wrapped in a `try-except` block, it will crash the entire function, even though the chapters were successfully fetched and could still be returned.

Wrapping the write operation in a `try-except OSError` block ensures that caching failures do not disrupt the primary functionality of the extractor.

```suggestion
        if archive_path_json:
            try:
                archive_path_json.write_text(
                    json.dumps(chapters_json),
                    encoding="utf-8",
                )
            except OSError as exc:
                logger.warning("Failed to write archived PCI chapters %s: %s", archive_path_json, exc)
```

